{"id": "EUVD-2026-76254", "enisaUuid": "82d3eb4b-dd6d-3931-809d-91c5559e5043", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nw1: ds28e17: reject an oversize length on an I2C block read\n\nw1_f19_i2c_master_transfer() is the master_xfer for the DS28E17 1-Wire\nto I2C bridge. On an I2C_M_RECV_LEN read, it takes the length from the\ndevice. The downstream slave puts a length byte in buf[0]. The driver\nthen reads that many bytes into buf[1] with w1_f19_i2c_read().\n\nbuf[0] is controlled by the device and can be 0 to 255.\nw1_f19_i2c_read() only rejects a zero count. The caller buffer is\nI2C_SMBUS_BLOCK_MAX + 2, so 34 bytes. A length above 32 makes the read\nrun past it, up to about 222 bytes out of bounds.\n\nThe SMBus core does check buf[0] against I2C_SMBUS_BLOCK_MAX. That\ncheck runs after master_xfer returns. By then the write is already\ndone. i2c-algo-bit rejects an oversize length before it copies, and\nreturns -EPROTO.\n\nReject a length above I2C_SMBUS_BLOCK_MAX at both RECV_LEN sites, the\nsame way i2c-algo-bit does.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:15", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b30c021c6073559ea6851b522d8a17a524a27b4a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d08877fc37e90945df38d255715bd1d6c052d46", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf76d61e118b7044600a65775a3bf8adc2c6823d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f6496b34cc2919420f303b2aabdd9f71e084b56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb55c5da9828f77db2a2701316949d4de1e9b773", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae0c79a8527044e54d81fd5a3b49ce6177633758", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6df05f630c84a109736642362e452089886f9974", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/169ae5e65e5aaf213b6a578f6478a9fd2e523606"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80931", "GHSA-3cwq-59j3-h9hj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4adc5e61-082c-30e3-8da5-73aa704000eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15"}, {"id": "4b89e39e-8668-3255-a412-74a457aa8183", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "5bc80be3-d705-3bc5-b94e-819008c53fa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ebc4768ac4971eab4b570e733e47ac9dfd0e4175 <0f6496b34cc2919420f303b2aabdd9f71e084b56"}, {"id": "87ab977e-504d-37df-81c5-910c7dfc9b18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "90918729-1c49-34d2-865b-143ce7218f25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ebc4768ac4971eab4b570e733e47ac9dfd0e4175 <1d08877fc37e90945df38d255715bd1d6c052d46"}, {"id": "916c4944-36ce-343a-950c-6b0881634c55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "a339ebe5-2d5b-30c5-b4a4-be3a524ee41a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ebc4768ac4971eab4b570e733e47ac9dfd0e4175 <6df05f630c84a109736642362e452089886f9974"}, {"id": "b0b961f1-bee5-3ec7-91c0-c33aaa51d225", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "b5945b13-4f9e-3311-8d8b-c40918e61c74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ebc4768ac4971eab4b570e733e47ac9dfd0e4175 <bf76d61e118b7044600a65775a3bf8adc2c6823d"}, {"id": "b5b82d5d-6c53-3ce4-8b6b-de351ed52c01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "c19406af-b0a2-3d35-8f24-4f2071178945", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c3ce1e79-3327-306d-ad17-b0fad6aebb04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "c